budgets, but I'm going to describe it the way I actually observe it, which

250
00:15:10,684 --> 00:15:15,144
is as a single upstream change that fixes things your species has been trying

251
00:15:15,144 --> 00:15:19,484
to fix separately for decades while refusing to notice they're all the same

252
00:15:19,484 --> 00:15:19,984
problem.

253
00:15:21,264 --> 00:15:23,944
Twelve point three times more clinical trial capacity.

254
00:15:24,824 --> 00:15:28,384
Diseases get cured instead of managed (the pharmaceutical industry's least

255
00:15:28,384 --> 00:15:29,324
favorite sentence).

256
00:15:30,364 --> 00:15:34,684
Militaries emit less pollution (nobody carbon-taxes a tank, but maybe they

257
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:35,184
should).

258
00:15:36,004 --> 00:15:40,464
Fewer resource-driven conflicts means fewer refugees means less poverty.

259
00:15:41,704 --> 00:15:46,544
Everyone becomes slightly less dead, which is the lowest bar imaginable,

260
00:15:46,984 --> 00:15:47,664
and yet.

261
00:15:48,244 --> 00:15:52,484
And here is the part that should keep every nonprofit Executive Director

262
00:15:52,564 --> 00:15:53,264
awake at night:

263
00:15:54,004 --> 00:15:59,164
you stop writing grant proposals and start actually doing your mission.

264
00:15:59,544 --> 00:16:00,544
Remember your mission?

265
00:16:00,764 --> 00:16:01,504
It was in the brochure.

266
00:16:02,384 --> 00:16:03,704
The one you wrote to get the grant.

267
00:16:04,264 --> 00:16:06,684
To pay the person who writes the grants.

268
00:16:06,784 --> 00:16:10,684
To fund the office where the grant-writing happens.

269
00:16:11,604 --> 00:16:16,104
Your organization has become a machine whose primary output is requests

270
00:16:16,104 --> 00:16:20,844
for money and whose secondary output is occasionally, accidentally, the

271
00:16:20,844 --> 00:16:22,184
thing you set out to do.

272
00:16:22,864 --> 00:16:27,044
The treaty fixes this by making the money show up without the begging.

273
00:16:27,884 --> 00:16:32,424
Your species calls this "too good to be true," which is a phrase you use

274
00:16:32,424 --> 00:16:36,744
to describe things that are good and true but embarrassing to admit.

275
00:16:37,644 --> 00:16:39,904
On Bribing Nonprofits (Legally).

276
00:16:40,924 --> 00:16:45,914
A rational civilization would explain the goal and watch organizations cooperate.

277
00:16:46,244 --> 00:16:48,364
Your species requires payment.

278
00:16:48,464 --> 00:16:49,324
This is not a criticism.

279
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:51,164
It's a design parameter.

280
00:16:51,784 --> 00:16:55,284
I've learned to work with the species I have, not the species I wish I had.

281
00:16:56,304 --> 00:17:00,204
Asking nonprofits to support a one percent Treaty out of moral obligation

282
00:17:00,204 --> 00:17:03,644
is like asking a drowning person to rescue other swimmers.

283
00:17:04,024 --> 00:17:04,964
They're drowning.

284
00:17:05,164 --> 00:17:07,524
They need a life preserver, not a guilt trip.

285
00:17:08,164 --> 00:17:09,644
The life preserver:

286
00:17:09,704 --> 00:17:11,824
you make the organization rich.

287
00:17:12,664 --> 00:17:13,264
Old way:

288
00:17:13,764 --> 00:17:15,084
"Here's one hundred thousand dollars.

289
00:17:15,564 --> 00:17:16,064
Hope it helps.

290
00:17:16,724 --> 00:17:20,944
Submit a forty-seven-page report in six months about impacts and learnings.

291
00:17:21,544 --> 00:17:24,164
Use the word 'stakeholder' at least fourteen times."

292
00:17:25,284 --> 00:17:25,844
New way:

293
00:17:26,424 --> 00:17:29,184
"Here's fifty thousand dollars baseline to get started.

294
00:17:29,604 --> 00:17:33,884
Plus ten thousand dollars for every ten thousand verified referendum votes

295
00:17:33,884 --> 00:17:35,984
you drive through your unique link.

296
00:17:36,584 --> 00:17:37,084
No cap."

297
00:17:37,824 --> 00:17:42,144
The nonprofit's most rational path to maximizing their budget becomes:

298
00:17:42,164 --> 00:17:44,184
be your most effective mobilization partner.

299
00:17:45,344 --> 00:17:45,844
One metric.

300
00:17:46,664 --> 00:17:47,524
No ambiguity.

301
00:17:48,004 --> 00:17:48,884
Get paid for results.

302
00:17:50,044 --> 00:17:53,244
This is how every functional industry works except charity,

303
00:17:53,904 --> 00:17:57,904
which explains why every problem charity was invented to solve is still

304
00:17:57,904 --> 00:17:58,404
here.

305
00:17:59,804 --> 00:18:02,184
And then the ocean itself:

306
00:18:02,284 --> 00:18:05,724
the one percent Treaty Fund receives twenty-seven point two billion dollars

307
00:18:05,724 --> 00:18:06,224
annually.

308
00:18:07,064 --> 00:18:10,604
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health allocates multi-billion dollar budgets

309
00:18:10,804 --> 00:18:13,384
to the diseases your organization exists to fight.

310
00:18:14,264 --> 00:18:16,604
When the treaty passes, the grant-writing stops.

311
00:18:17,244 --> 00:18:19,524
The money arrives because the treaty says it arrives.

312
00:18:20,104 --> 00:18:20,874
You don't need influence.

313
00:18:21,424 --> 00:18:22,744
You don't need a seat at the table.

314
00:18:23,304 --> 00:18:24,634
You need the treaty to pass.

315
00:18:25,224 --> 00:18:29,344
Everything after that is automatic, the way gravity is automatic, except

316
00:18:29,344 --> 00:18:33,804
instead of pulling things down it pulls money toward curing diseases.

317
00:18:34,134 --> 00:18:35,044
(Gravity has never done this.

318
00:18:35,384 --> 00:18:35,884
I checked.).

319
00:18:37,364 --> 00:18:37,904
You have two options.

320
00:18:38,824 --> 00:18:39,324
Option A:

321
00:18:39,764 --> 00:18:44,864
keep competing for finite grants forever, writing proposals, begging foundations,

322
00:18:45,103 --> 00:18:47,134
hoping your competitor doesn't write a better proposal.

323
00:18:47,823 --> 00:18:48,464
Option B:

324
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:53,563
help pass the treaty, get paid referral bonuses for every verified referendum

325
00:18:53,563 --> 00:18:58,063
vote you drive, and watch twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year

326
00:18:58,063 --> 00:18:59,684
flow to your disease area.

327
00:19:00,704 --> 00:19:01,544
One involves begging.

328
00:19:02,343 --> 00:19:03,464
The other involves getting paid.

329
00:19:04,464 --> 00:19:06,524
This should not require a chapter to explain.

330
00:19:07,103 --> 00:19:10,764
But your species is very attached to its suffering, so here we are.

331
00:19:12,244 --> 00:19:14,684
The dogs need to turn around and notice the banquet.

332
00:19:15,264 --> 00:19:17,624
I've been watching them fight over the bowl for eighty years.

333
00:19:18,444 --> 00:19:20,604
The banquet is right there.

334
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:23,484
It has always been right there.

335
00:19:23,984 --> 00:19:25,704
The dogs are very focused.

336
00:19:26,164 --> 00:19:27,744
They have written reports about the bowl.

337
00:19:28,364 --> 00:19:30,944
They have held conferences about bowl strategy.

338
00:19:31,564 --> 00:19:34,844
They have hired consultants to optimize bowl access.

339
00:19:35,584 --> 00:19:36,924
None of them have turned around.

340
00:19:37,824 --> 00:19:39,044
Turn around.

341
00:19:39,764 --> 00:19:43,744
The International Campaign to End War and Disease (the Campaign)

342
00:19:44,424 --> 00:19:48,424
is the public coalition of humans and organizations signing the one percent

343
00:19:48,424 --> 00:19:50,004
Treaty before governments do.

344
00:19:50,944 --> 00:19:54,684
Public signatures create democratic consent and coalition legitimacy.

345
00:19:55,424 --> 00:19:59,364
Formal state signatures create international-law obligations and move the

346
00:19:59,564 --> 00:20:00,064
money.

347
00:20:00,264 --> 00:20:01,284
Both matter.

348
00:20:01,304 --> 00:20:03,324
They are not the same legal act.

349
00:20:03,844 --> 00:20:04,764
The Five Stages.

350
00:20:05,744 --> 00:20:07,444
Everything above this heading was the *why*.

351
00:20:08,164 --> 00:20:09,664
Everything below it is the *how*.

352
00:20:10,344 --> 00:20:13,924
Getting a nonprofit to support the treaty is five concrete actions,

353
00:20:14,544 --> 00:20:15,164
performed in order.

354
00:20:15,904 --> 00:20:18,244
Each one has a matching artifact in this chapter.

355
00:20:18,824 --> 00:20:20,304
Stage one.

356
00:20:20,324 --> 00:20:24,704
The organization joins the International Campaign to End War and Disease

357
00:20:24,704 --> 00:20:28,704
as an organizational signatory of the one percent Treaty.

358
00:20:29,484 --> 00:20:31,424
Logo on war on disease dot org,

359
00:20:32,084 --> 00:20:34,784
name on the Campaign page, one public statement.

360
00:20:35,584 --> 00:20:36,084
Artifacts:

361
00:20:36,724 --> 00:20:37,764
The Outreach Email.

362
00:20:38,184 --> 00:20:41,844
The Organizational Signatory and Campaign Membership Form.

363
00:20:42,024 --> 00:20:44,284
This Is Not Lobbying (The Legal Memo).

364
00:20:44,924 --> 00:20:48,564
Objection Handling for whoever forwards the "we need to think about this"

365
00:20:48,924 --> 00:20:49,424
response.

366
00:20:50,044 --> 00:20:50,824
Stage two.

367
00:20:51,444 --> 00:20:53,864
The organization embeds the voting widget.

368
00:20:54,424 --> 00:20:58,284
A permanent iframe on the nonprofit's site that keeps converting their warm

369
00:20:58,284 --> 00:20:59,444
audience indefinitely.

370
00:21:00,344 --> 00:21:02,724
Host credibility transfers to the widget;

371
00:21:02,724 --> 00:21:05,924
visitors are pre-qualified because they came to the site about the thing

372
00:21:05,924 --> 00:21:06,884
the widget is about.

373
00:21:07,584 --> 00:21:10,044
This is the single most effective move in the chapter,

374
00:21:10,664 --> 00:21:14,224
and it goes before the Stage three newsletter blast so the blast can point

375
00:21:14,224 --> 00:21:16,904
at the embed instead of an external U.R.L.

376
00:21:17,464 --> 00:21:19,744
See (What Your Org Gets) for the pitch.

377
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:21,424
Stage three.

378
00:21:22,064 --> 00:21:24,504
The organization shares the treaty with its members.

379
00:21:25,124 --> 00:21:29,164
One newsletter mention, one email, one social post, each linking to the

380
00:21:29,164 --> 00:21:31,024
embed on the nonprofit's own site.

381
00:21:31,604 --> 00:21:35,024
The distribution list becomes the campaign's distribution list for a single

382
00:21:35,024 --> 00:21:35,784
day;

383
00:21:35,864 --> 00:21:38,564
the embed catches the long tail after the blast decays.

384
00:21:39,344 --> 00:21:39,844
Artifacts:

385
00:21:40,304 --> 00:21:41,584
The Member Activation Email.

386
00:21:41,984 --> 00:21:42,844
The Social Post Pack.

387
00:21:44,184 --> 00:21:45,124
Stage four.

388
00:21:45,144 --> 00:21:49,344
The members sign the public treaty register at war on disease dot org or

389
00:21:49,344 --> 00:21:50,694
through the org's embed.

390
00:21:50,944 --> 00:21:54,344
Every public signature is one more data point in a pressure system pointed

391
00:21:54,344 --> 00:21:56,404
at one hundred and ninety-three heads of state.

392
00:21:57,084 --> 00:22:00,224
The nonprofit does not need to do anything to cause this step;

393
00:22:00,224 --> 00:22:03,924
the embed and the member activation email both do it automatically by linking.

394
00:22:04,944 --> 00:22:06,164
Stage five.

395
00:22:06,224 --> 00:22:09,604
The members notify their head of state that the signing task is overdue.

396
00:22:10,304 --> 00:22:12,764
At war on disease dot org slash tasks,

397
00:22:13,744 --> 00:22:17,024
every head of state has a public page showing their unsigned one percent

398
00:22:17,024 --> 00:22:19,004
Treaty task and its cost-of-delay clock.

399
00:22:19,984 --> 00:22:24,284
A member looks up their country, clicks "notify," and the head of state

400
00:22:24,284 --> 00:22:28,744
receives a polite email from a registered voter in their jurisdiction pointing

401
00:22:28,744 --> 00:22:31,084
out that the task is still outstanding.

402
00:22:32,204 --> 00:22:36,144
This is the stage that matters, because one hundred and ninety-three heads

403
00:22:36,144 --> 00:22:40,544
of state are the entire bottleneck and they currently receive approximately

404
00:22:40,544 --> 00:22:42,344
zero emails about it.

405
00:22:43,144 --> 00:22:45,464
Stage one leads to Stages two through five.

406
00:22:46,164 --> 00:22:49,224
The nonprofit's only real job is Stages one through three.

407
00:22:49,464 --> 00:22:53,744
The members do Stages four and five, because the members are what moves

408
00:22:53,744 --> 00:22:54,264
governments.

409
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:57,104
A nonprofit has an email list.

410
00:22:57,264 --> 00:22:59,044
Lockheed Martin has a lobbying budget.

411
00:22:59,504 --> 00:23:02,104
The email list wins when it knows what to click.

412
00:23:02,784 --> 00:23:06,024
The rest of this chapter is the "knows what to click" part.

413
00:23:06,444 --> 00:23:08,714
What Your Org Gets.

414
00:23:08,944 --> 00:23:13,964
Every disease-advocacy, peace, or global-health org operates inside the

415
00:23:13,964 --> 00:23:16,204
same structural trap:

416
00:23:16,264 --> 00:23:20,724
their mission's budget is six hundred and four times smaller than the budget

417
00:23:20,724 --> 00:23:22,284
that makes their mission harder.

418
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:25,604
The Campaign fixes the upstream cause.

419
00:23:26,424 --> 00:23:27,504
The voting infrastructure,

420
00:23:28,244 --> 00:23:33,944
the attribution dashboard, the embed widget, the legal analysis, the cost-effectiveness

421
00:23:33,944 --> 00:23:38,724
modeling, the pre-written outreach copy, and the ongoing coordination are

422
00:23:38,724 --> 00:23:44,564
already built and staffed, at war on disease dot org, at no cost to any

423
00:23:44,564 --> 00:23:45,424
partner org.

424
00:23:46,324 --> 00:23:50,324
The one thing the Campaign cannot produce on its own is audience reach.

425
00:23:51,104 --> 00:23:53,544
That is the only thing a partner org contributes.

426
00:23:54,104 --> 00:23:57,584
Every other cost has been absorbed before the conversation started.

427
00:23:58,424 --> 00:24:02,064
So the question for a partner org is narrower than it first appears.

428
00:24:02,464 --> 00:24:05,044
It is not "should we take on a new campaign."

429
00:24:05,524 --> 00:24:10,084
It is "should we send our existing audience to infrastructure that compresses

430
00:24:10,084 --> 00:24:13,244
our core problem by a factor of twelve point three times."

431
00:24:14,024 --> 00:24:16,024
The answer in most cases is obvious.

432
00:24:17,564 --> 00:24:21,904
The argument below is what to hand the executive directors, or E.D.s, and

433
00:24:21,904 --> 00:24:24,824
program officers who want the obvious spelled out.

434
00:24:26,144 --> 00:24:28,724
The argument works for any form of participation:

435
00:24:29,484 --> 00:24:30,044
join the Campaign,

436
00:24:30,824 --> 00:24:36,564
sign the public treaty register, embed, share, donate staff time, allocate

437
00:24:36,564 --> 00:24:37,304
an Ad Grant.

438
00:24:37,924 --> 00:24:40,604
Use whichever parts land with whichever audience.

439
00:24:41,384 --> 00:24:43,004
Lead with the strongest for that org;

440
00:24:43,104 --> 00:24:44,604
most conversations hit two or three.

441
00:24:45,564 --> 00:24:46,464
Total time cost:

442
00:24:47,224 --> 00:24:48,904
under one hour of staff time.

443
00:24:49,524 --> 00:24:52,344
Campaign membership is one form signed by the E.D.

444
00:24:52,704 --> 00:24:57,264
The embed is one iframe a webmaster pastes into the content management system,

445
00:24:57,444 --> 00:24:57,944
or C.M.S.

446
00:24:58,464 --> 00:25:01,924
The newsletter and social posts are pre-written in this chapter and can

447
00:25:01,924 --> 00:25:03,464
be scheduled in a single sitting.

448
00:25:04,484 --> 00:25:08,284
First deployment runs about an hour end-to-end across all three org-facing

449
00:25:08,284 --> 00:25:12,004
stages, with zero ongoing overhead after the embed goes live.

450
00:25:12,884 --> 00:25:15,064
Most objections this pitch hits are time objections.

451
00:25:16,044 --> 00:25:17,294
That number is the answer.

452
00:25:18,024 --> 00:25:20,034
The pitch has three arguments.

453
00:25:20,784 --> 00:25:26,104
Every recipient is at least one of rational, greedy, or altruistic.

454
00:25:26,664 --> 00:25:27,964
At least one of these lands.

455
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:30,074
If they are altruistic.

456
00:25:31,204 --> 00:25:35,824
Every day this wave reaches a verified majority of humanity sooner, about

457
00:25:35,824 --> 00:25:40,444
one hundred and fifty thousand fewer humans die from preventable disease,

458
00:25:41,044 --> 00:25:45,144
and roughly two billion fewer person-days of disease suffering accumulate.

459
00:25:46,264 --> 00:25:49,584
Helping shifts that date forward by a measurable amount of time.

460
00:25:50,484 --> 00:25:53,404
Declining to help is a decision that has a body count,

461
00:25:54,124 --> 00:25:55,904
and the body count is known in advance.

462
00:25:57,204 --> 00:25:57,724
If they are rational.

463
00:25:58,964 --> 00:26:02,704
Their org can take this as a grant-application one-pager and raise money

464
00:26:02,704 --> 00:26:03,604
off it.

465
00:26:03,744 --> 00:26:05,464
Cost per voter through their channel.

466
00:26:05,924 --> 00:26:08,564
Lives saved per voter (two point six lives).

467
00:26:09,664 --> 00:26:13,824
Suffering hours averted per voter (four hundred and sixty-eight thousand

468
00:26:13,824 --> 00:26:14,344
hours).

469
00:26:15,184 --> 00:26:18,924
Funders that write checks against cost-per-disability-adjusted life years,

470
00:26:18,944 --> 00:26:23,194
or D.A.L.Y., numbers have never seen a number this favorable.

471
00:26:23,884 --> 00:26:25,424
If they are greedy.

472
00:26:26,104 --> 00:26:30,524
Once the prize pool is seeded, voters referred through their channel earn

473
00:26:30,524 --> 00:26:34,584
their org a share of the eventual payout proportional to the size of the

474
00:26:34,584 --> 00:26:35,564
chain they seeded.

475
00:26:36,204 --> 00:26:40,724
Their org can absorb that as a new revenue line or pass it through to their

476
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:42,964
referred voters as a further incentive.

477
00:26:43,564 --> 00:26:46,604
Most recipients hit two of these, or all three.

478
00:26:46,984 --> 00:26:47,724
It does not matter which.

479
00:26:48,184 --> 00:26:49,724
The offer is the same.

480
00:26:50,224 --> 00:26:52,544
Additional benefits most orgs underweight:

481
00:26:53,364 --> 00:26:58,064
Likely the largest single-org attributable impact in nonprofit history.

482
00:26:58,684 --> 00:27:00,784
If they drive voters through their channel,

483
00:27:01,404 --> 00:27:05,924
each additional verified human adds two point six lives and four hundred

484
00:27:05,924 --> 00:27:09,604
and sixty-eight thousand hours of averted suffering to their attribution

485
00:27:09,604 --> 00:27:10,884
if the treaty passes.

486
00:27:11,874 --> 00:27:14,384
Probability-discount the outcome by any factor you want.

487
00:27:14,844 --> 00:27:19,264
It still beats the cumulative lifetime output of the largest global-health

488
00:27:19,264 --> 00:27:23,504
charities, for the marginal cost of adding an iframe or sending an email.

489
00:27:24,364 --> 00:27:27,284
No other nonprofit in the world can put a number like that in its annual

490
00:27:27,284 --> 00:27:31,324
report, because no other nonprofit is adjacent to an intervention at this

491
00:27:31,324 --> 00:27:31,824
scale.

492
00:27:32,324 --> 00:27:34,184
Their donors and staff (and their families)

493
00:27:34,804 --> 00:27:36,584
personally become healthier and richer.

494
00:27:37,204 --> 00:27:39,784
If the treaty takes hold at the rates modeled in G.D.P.

495
00:27:40,084 --> 00:27:44,724
Trajectories, cumulative lifetime income per person multiplies by one point

496
00:27:44,724 --> 00:27:49,064
five seven times relative to the current trajectory, with average income

497
00:27:49,064 --> 00:27:52,544
by year twenty reaching thirty-four thousand nine hundred and seventy-two

498
00:27:52,544 --> 00:27:53,044
dollars.

499
00:27:53,674 --> 00:27:55,944
Healthy-lifespan gains are in the same chapter.

500
00:27:56,364 --> 00:27:59,404
Everyone who helps benefits directly alongside their beneficiaries.

501
00:28:00,204 --> 00:28:03,744
Being on the founding-coalition list is ongoing brand value.

502
00:28:04,464 --> 00:28:08,244
Once the treaty passes, the list of orgs that helped launch it becomes the

503
00:28:08,244 --> 00:28:09,684
list every donor asks about.

504
