602
00:33:27,464 --> 00:33:28,404
What the words mean.

603
00:33:29,604 --> 00:33:30,364
Public signature.

604
00:33:30,924 --> 00:33:34,424
A human or organization signs the public treaty register.

605
00:33:35,164 --> 00:33:38,404
This creates democratic consent and coalition legitimacy.

606
00:33:39,304 --> 00:33:40,824
Organizational signatory.

607
00:33:41,604 --> 00:33:46,784
A nonprofit, company, union, school, church, or other institution joins

608
00:33:46,784 --> 00:33:51,644
the International Campaign to End War and Disease and publicly signs the

609
00:33:51,644 --> 00:33:54,624
one percent Treaty as an organizational supporter.

610
00:33:55,504 --> 00:33:56,684
Formal state signature.

611
00:33:57,484 --> 00:34:02,064
A government signs or ratifies the treaty through its ordinary international-law

612
00:34:02,064 --> 00:34:02,584
process.

613
00:34:03,184 --> 00:34:05,704
This creates Article one funding obligations.

614
00:34:06,784 --> 00:34:07,444
Treaty party.

615
00:34:08,104 --> 00:34:09,784
A state bound by the treaty.

616
00:34:10,524 --> 00:34:15,044
Nonprofits are not treaty parties and do not assume government budget obligations.

617
00:34:15,844 --> 00:34:17,124
What the I.R.S.

618
00:34:17,204 --> 00:34:18,244
defines as lobbying.

619
00:34:19,204 --> 00:34:24,484
Under Internal Revenue Code, or I.R.C., section five oh one c three, "lobbying"

620
00:34:24,704 --> 00:34:30,164
means attempting to influence specific domestic legislation (a bill, resolution,

621
00:34:30,324 --> 00:34:31,784
or act before a legislative body).

622
00:34:33,164 --> 00:34:33,964
The I.R.S.

623
00:34:33,964 --> 00:34:35,844
applies two tests:

624
00:34:35,844 --> 00:34:36,584
Direct lobbying.

625
00:34:37,364 --> 00:34:40,984
Communicating with a legislator about specific legislation and expressing

626
00:34:40,984 --> 00:34:41,824
a view on it.

627
00:34:42,644 --> 00:34:43,664
Grassroots lobbying.

628
00:34:44,364 --> 00:34:46,914
Communicating with the public about specific legislation,

629
00:34:47,564 --> 00:34:51,624
expressing a view, and including a call to action directed at legislators.

630
00:34:52,604 --> 00:34:55,984
The Campaign's public-signature work meets neither definition.

631
00:34:56,984 --> 00:34:59,544
Why treaty advocacy is not lobbying.

632
00:35:00,464 --> 00:35:02,824
The treaty is not domestic legislation.

633
00:35:03,564 --> 00:35:07,484
The one percent Treaty is a proposed international agreement between sovereign

634
00:35:07,484 --> 00:35:07,984
nations.

635
00:35:08,484 --> 00:35:11,854
It is not a bill before any domestic legislative body.

636
00:35:12,504 --> 00:35:13,164
Under I.R.S.

637
00:35:13,244 --> 00:35:17,224
guidelines this is categorized as issue advocacy, not lobbying.

638
00:35:18,384 --> 00:35:21,144
The Campaign does not ask anything of domestic legislators.

639
00:35:22,004 --> 00:35:26,824
The ask is directed at heads of state, who sign international agreements

640
00:35:26,824 --> 00:35:29,344
as executives, not legislators.

641
00:35:30,104 --> 00:35:32,824
There is no "call your congressperson" component.

642
00:35:33,524 --> 00:35:36,104
No specific domestic legislation is referenced.

643
00:35:37,064 --> 00:35:39,824
The Campaign does not support or oppose candidates.

644
00:35:40,724 --> 00:35:45,864
The accountability dashboard at war on disease dot org slash tasks tracks

645
00:35:45,864 --> 00:35:48,123
treaty signature status by head of state.

646
00:35:48,904 --> 00:35:52,824
This is functionally identical to how Transparency International publishes

647
00:35:52,824 --> 00:35:54,304
corruption indices by country.

648
00:35:55,444 --> 00:35:59,163
Publishing factual information about government performance is core five

649
00:35:59,163 --> 00:36:00,814
oh one c three educational activity.

650
00:36:01,764 --> 00:36:04,604
Even if classified as lobbying, it would be permitted.

651
00:36:05,623 --> 00:36:09,064
Five oh one c three organizations can lobby up to twenty percent of their

652
00:36:09,064 --> 00:36:11,064
budget under the five oh one h election.

653
00:36:11,884 --> 00:36:15,944
A public treaty signature and organizational signature are vastly below

654
00:36:15,944 --> 00:36:19,104
any threshold any interpretation could trigger.

655
00:36:19,623 --> 00:36:20,424
Historical precedent.

656
00:36:21,123 --> 00:36:25,784
No five-oh-one (c)(three) has ever lost its tax-exempt status for advocating

657
00:36:25,784 --> 00:36:27,163
for a global treaty.

658
00:36:27,924 --> 00:36:28,623
The I.R.S.

659
00:36:28,623 --> 00:36:33,223
has revoked status for fraud, private inurement, failure to file Form nine

660
00:36:33,223 --> 00:36:37,344
hundred and ninety for three consecutive years, and excessive partisan political

661
00:36:37,344 --> 00:36:38,104
activity.

662
00:36:39,064 --> 00:36:42,294
Treaty advocacy has never been a basis for revocation.

663
00:36:43,184 --> 00:36:46,804
Multiple five-oh-one (c)(three) organizations actively campaign for international

664
00:36:46,804 --> 00:36:47,564
treaties.

665
00:36:48,304 --> 00:36:52,084
The International Campaign to Ban Landmines, a coalition of five-oh-one

666
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:52,584
(c)(three)s,

667
00:36:53,184 --> 00:36:56,484
led the campaign that produced the Ottawa Treaty in nineteen ninety-seven

668
00:36:56,484 --> 00:36:59,284
and won the Nobel Peace Prize for it.

669
00:36:59,824 --> 00:37:03,884
Physicians for Social Responsibility advocates for the Treaty on the Prohibition

670
00:37:03,884 --> 00:37:05,084
of Nuclear Weapons.

671
00:37:05,824 --> 00:37:09,424
Human Rights Watch campaigns for international human rights treaties.

672
00:37:09,944 --> 00:37:13,934
Oxfam America advocates for international trade and arms treaties.

673
00:37:14,424 --> 00:37:15,964
None have faced I.R.S.

674
00:37:15,964 --> 00:37:17,584
action for their treaty advocacy.

