00:59:48,484 --> 00:59:52,004
Maximum funder exposure is five thousand dollars plus the rate times the

1105
00:59:52,004 --> 00:59:52,504
target.

1106
00:59:53,124 --> 00:59:56,824
At one dollar per voter, it is fifteen thousand dollars for ten thousand

1107
00:59:56,824 --> 01:00:00,944
voters, one hundred and five thousand dollars for one hundred thousand voters,

1108
01:00:01,364 --> 01:00:05,004
and one million five thousand dollars for one million voters.

1109
01:00:05,724 --> 01:00:09,184
Delivery is public through the war on disease dot org dashboard;

1110
01:00:09,404 --> 01:00:13,324
the funder pays monthly in arrears against voters actually delivered, never

1111
01:00:13,324 --> 01:00:13,824
advanced.

1112
01:00:14,784 --> 01:00:16,744
Close every proposal with:

1113
01:00:16,744 --> 01:00:20,754
"What per-voter rate and delivery target would make this the best cost-per-D.A.L.Y.

1114
01:00:21,324 --> 01:00:22,724
grant in your current portfolio,

1115
01:00:23,404 --> 01:00:26,124
and if we can hit it, is there any blocker to signing?".

1116
01:00:27,624 --> 01:00:28,504
Outreach Sequencing.

1117
01:00:29,504 --> 01:00:30,004
Five steps.

1118
01:00:30,484 --> 01:00:31,244
Do them in order.

1119
01:00:32,784 --> 01:00:33,284
Step one.

1120
01:00:33,844 --> 01:00:35,744
Identify warm contacts (week one).

1121
01:00:36,424 --> 01:00:39,844
List every organization the outreach person has a prior relationship with.

1122
01:00:40,544 --> 01:00:44,484
Prioritize by strength of relationship (will they respond?), mission alignment

1123
01:00:44,484 --> 01:00:49,554
(disease, health, longevity, peace, poverty), and community size.

1124
01:00:50,424 --> 01:00:50,924
Step two.

1125
01:00:51,364 --> 01:00:53,664
Get the first three yeses (weeks one to three).

1126
01:00:54,824 --> 01:00:57,024
Contact the three to five warmest relationships first.

1127
01:00:57,944 --> 01:00:59,044
Use "The Outreach Email".

1128
01:01:00,164 --> 01:01:04,804
The goal is logos on the coalition page before going wide, because social

1129
01:01:04,804 --> 01:01:05,964
proof compounds.

1130
01:01:06,404 --> 01:01:07,824
Step three.

1131
01:01:08,424 --> 01:01:11,144
Go wide with social proof (weeks three to eight).

1132
01:01:12,084 --> 01:01:15,944
Once there are founding members, update the outreach email to include "X

1133
01:01:15,944 --> 01:01:19,204
organizations are already on board, including names."

1134
01:01:20,184 --> 01:01:23,144
Contact over two hundred organizations in batches of fifty.

1135
01:01:24,104 --> 01:01:25,824
Track responses in a simple spreadsheet.

1136
01:01:26,664 --> 01:01:29,464
Note the organization name and the contact person.

1137
01:01:29,884 --> 01:01:32,264
Track the date contacted and the response received.

1138
01:01:33,104 --> 01:01:36,164
Include columns for the follow-up date and whether they have signed.

1139
01:01:37,184 --> 01:01:38,864
Mark whether the logo has been received.

1140
01:01:40,044 --> 01:01:41,084
Step four.

1141
01:01:41,124 --> 01:01:42,284
Follow up (ongoing).

1142
01:01:43,284 --> 01:01:44,704
No response after five days:

1143
01:01:45,204 --> 01:01:45,944
one short follow-up.

1144
01:01:47,004 --> 01:01:48,464
No response after ten days:

1145
01:01:48,884 --> 01:01:50,224
one more, even shorter.

1146
01:01:51,004 --> 01:01:52,804
No response after fifteen days:

1147
01:01:53,144 --> 01:01:53,644
move on.

1148
01:01:54,704 --> 01:01:55,604
"We need to think":

1149
01:01:56,424 --> 01:01:57,084
follow up in two weeks.

1150
01:01:58,004 --> 01:01:58,884
"We have concerns":

1151
01:01:59,384 --> 01:02:00,474
offer a call immediately.

1152
01:02:01,444 --> 01:02:03,344
"What would we need to change?":

1153
01:02:03,344 --> 01:02:04,544
the most valuable response.

1154
01:02:05,264 --> 01:02:07,204
Incorporate reasonable feedback;

1155
01:02:07,204 --> 01:02:08,884
reject changes that gut the substance.

1156
01:02:10,284 --> 01:02:11,244
Step five.

1157
01:02:11,304 --> 01:02:13,764
Announce the coalition (months two to three).

1158
01:02:14,764 --> 01:02:17,184
Once there are ten or more organizational signatories:

1159
01:02:18,424 --> 01:02:20,284
Publish the coalition page with logos.

1160
01:02:21,144 --> 01:02:21,944
Write a press release.

1161
01:02:22,744 --> 01:02:25,204
Have each founding member share with its community.

1162
01:02:26,064 --> 01:02:26,864
Submit to the E.A.

1163
01:02:27,164 --> 01:02:29,564
Forum with economist sign-on if available.

1164
01:02:30,024 --> 01:02:30,964
Objection Handling.

1165
01:02:31,664 --> 01:02:34,384
The top objections, with the top answer to each.

1166
01:02:35,244 --> 01:02:39,844
If the same objection keeps appearing, revise the outreach email so it preempts

1167
01:02:39,844 --> 01:02:40,344
it.

1168
01:02:40,924 --> 01:02:42,334
"This is too political."

1169
01:02:43,284 --> 01:02:47,924
The treaty specifies a simultaneous reduction, preserving military balance.

1170
01:02:48,664 --> 01:02:52,524
It does not favor or oppose any nation, party, or candidate.

1171
01:02:53,184 --> 01:02:57,204
It is no more political than advocating for increased N.I.H.

1172
01:02:57,224 --> 01:03:00,694
funding, which hundreds of five zero one c threes already do.

1173
01:03:01,464 --> 01:03:03,824
The underlying fact is not partisan:

1174
01:03:04,624 --> 01:03:08,284
everyone's lifetime risk of dying from a disease is one hundred percent,

1175
01:03:08,724 --> 01:03:10,964
and the current budget does not reflect this.

1176
01:03:11,864 --> 01:03:13,244
"This will never work."

1177
01:03:14,144 --> 01:03:18,564
The International Campaign to Ban Landmines started with one staff member

1178
01:03:18,564 --> 01:03:20,684
and six N.G.O.s in nineteen ninety-two.

1179
01:03:21,264 --> 01:03:24,664
By nineteen ninety-seven, one hundred and twenty-two nations signed the

1180
01:03:24,664 --> 01:03:27,924
Ottawa Treaty and the campaign won the Nobel Peace Prize.

1181
01:03:28,764 --> 01:03:31,424
A one percent cut is historically trivial:

1182
01:03:32,124 --> 01:03:33,764
pre-World War Two U.S.

1183
01:03:33,764 --> 01:03:38,144
military spending was ninety-six point seven percent lower than today's

1184
01:03:38,204 --> 01:03:38,764
peacetime budget.

1185
01:03:39,604 --> 01:03:41,444
After World War Two, the U.S.

1186
01:03:41,604 --> 01:03:46,384
cut military spending by eighty-seven percent point six percent in two years

1187
01:03:46,764 --> 01:03:49,624
and produced the largest economic boom in modern history.

1188
01:03:50,324 --> 01:03:54,864
A one percent simultaneous reduction is rounding error compared to what

1189
01:03:54,864 --> 01:03:56,044
has already been done safely.

1190
01:03:57,004 --> 01:03:58,484
"Our board won't approve this."

1191
01:03:59,524 --> 01:04:01,924
Send them This Is Not Lobbying (The Legal Memo).

1192
01:04:02,404 --> 01:04:03,964
It addresses every I.R.S.

1193
01:04:04,104 --> 01:04:04,604
concern.

1194
01:04:04,824 --> 01:04:08,324
Offer a twenty-minute call with the board, or a written memo tailored to

1195
01:04:08,324 --> 01:04:09,464
their specific bylaws.

1196
01:04:10,624 --> 01:04:12,014
"We don't want to link to that website."

1197
01:04:13,144 --> 01:04:14,144
Link to the treaty text itself.

1198
01:04:15,164 --> 01:04:18,944
Organizations sign the public treaty register and publicly support the treaty

1199
01:04:18,944 --> 01:04:19,464
Articles,

1200
01:04:20,124 --> 01:04:21,804
not any particular framing of them.

1201
01:04:22,144 --> 01:04:24,694
They can use whichever version they are comfortable with.

1202
01:04:25,704 --> 01:04:26,974
"We're too small to matter."

1203
01:04:27,984 --> 01:04:30,604
Every organizational signature adds social proof.

1204
01:04:31,124 --> 01:04:33,864
The first ten matter more than the next one hundred.

1205
01:04:34,964 --> 01:04:39,944
Small organizations that move fast become founding members, which is a permanently

1206
01:04:39,944 --> 01:04:43,124
better position than large organizations that move slow.

1207
01:04:44,624 --> 01:04:46,324
"What about our existing campaigns?"

1208
01:04:47,424 --> 01:04:51,844
This complements existing work and does not replace or compete with anything.

1209
01:04:52,584 --> 01:04:57,064
End-to-end first deployment is under one hour of staff time across all three

1210
01:04:57,064 --> 01:04:58,084
org-facing stages:

1211
01:04:58,664 --> 01:05:02,604
about fifteen minutes to sign, about thirty minutes for a webmaster to paste

1212
01:05:02,604 --> 01:05:06,964
the embed iframe into the C.M.S., and about fifteen minutes to schedule

1213
01:05:06,964 --> 01:05:10,004
the pre-written newsletter and social posts from this chapter.

1214
01:05:10,724 --> 01:05:14,744
After that, the embed converts passively with zero ongoing overhead.

1215
01:05:15,784 --> 01:05:17,884
Membership also opens a new funding line:

1216
01:05:18,524 --> 01:05:22,484
global-health, peace, and policy funders increasingly fund coalition work

1217
01:05:22,484 --> 01:05:25,744
on this issue, and coalition membership opens eligibility.

1218
01:05:26,944 --> 01:05:28,504
"The numbers seem too good to be true."

1219
01:05:29,264 --> 01:05:33,584
They are calculated with ninety-five percent confidence intervals and ninety-plus

1220
01:05:33,584 --> 01:05:34,384
cited sources.

1221
01:05:34,964 --> 01:05:38,384
The full methodology is transparent in the parameters and calculations appendix.

1222
01:05:39,324 --> 01:05:42,584
Offer to connect them with an economist reviewer, or invite them to review

1223
01:05:42,584 --> 01:05:43,524
the model themselves.

1224
01:05:44,504 --> 01:05:46,084
That is the whole chapter.

1225
01:05:46,784 --> 01:05:52,604
The outreach email bundles the full ask (sign, embed, share) with every

1226
01:05:52,604 --> 01:05:57,344
artifact attached, so first contact is also last contact for orgs that say

1227
01:05:57,344 --> 01:05:57,844
yes.

1228
01:05:58,444 --> 01:05:59,824
If an organization commits,

1229
01:06:00,564 --> 01:06:03,964
confirm the embed is live on their site and the newsletter is scheduled,

1230
01:06:04,384 --> 01:06:05,904
then move on to the next org.

1231
01:06:06,544 --> 01:06:11,044
If an organization declines, ask what would change their mind and what they

1232
01:06:11,044 --> 01:06:15,824
are doing with the same staff hours that beats this on cost per disability-adjusted

1233
01:06:15,824 --> 01:06:17,564
life years, or D.A.L.Y.s.

1234
01:06:18,284 --> 01:06:20,064
Incorporate useful feedback;

1235
01:06:20,064 --> 01:06:21,264
retry in sixty days.

1236
01:06:21,724 --> 01:06:25,264
If the same objection appears three times in a week, update the outreach

1237
01:06:25,264 --> 01:06:26,404
email to preempt it.

1238
01:06:27,124 --> 01:06:31,844
The bottleneck between here and five hundred and sixty-five billion D.A.L.Y.s

1239
01:06:31,844 --> 01:06:37,084
averted is not the math, the legal analysis, the templates, or the treaty

1240
01:06:37,084 --> 01:06:37,644
itself.

1241
01:06:38,364 --> 01:06:42,004
It is the number of organizations that have opened the conversation with

1242
01:06:42,004 --> 01:06:42,704
their members.

1243
01:06:43,284 --> 01:06:46,664
That number is a function of how many outreach emails get sent this week.

1244
01:06:47,364 --> 01:06:49,264
Do the next thing on the sequencing list.

1245
01:06:49,356 --> 01:06:54,896
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

1246
01:06:54,896 --> 01:06:59,116
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

1247
01:06:59,116 --> 01:07:02,816
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

1248
01:07:02,816 --> 01:07:03,856
war and disease instead.

1249
01:07:04,476 --> 01:07:08,816
